.TH MODBUS-FAKE-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-fake-ctl \- one-shot control client for the fake inverter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-fake-ctl
.RI [ options ]
.IB command " [args ...]"
.br
.B modbus-fake-ctl
.RI [ options ]
< commands
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one control command (or a batch piped on stdin, one per line) to the
.B modbus-fake-inverter
JSON-lines control server and prints the replies on stdout, one per line.
Every invocation lands in the audit trail (prefix \fBCTL\fR).
.PP
The command grammar is the fake's: \fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/
\fBhelp\fR (the 24-setting registry), \fBshow status\fR,
\fBshow settings\fR, \fBshow registers\fR, \fBshow version\fR,
\fBinspect\fR, \fBreset\fR, \fBshutdown\fR, \fBquit\fR. See
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1)
CONTROL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-control-port " TARGET"
the control target: a unix socket path or a TCP port. Default
\fB/tmp/fake-inverter-\fR\fI<modbus-port>\fB.socket\fR; the
\fBFAKE_CTL\fR environment variable is the same knob.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " S"
wire timeout, seconds. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-control-token " TOKEN" ", " \-\-control-token-file " FILE"
the token for TCP control (mutually exclusive).
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-log " FILE|\-"
the client's own audit trail
(\fB~/.local/state/fake-inverter/audit.log\fR by default).
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-max-mb " N ", \-\-audit-files " N"
the file sink's gated rotation (defaults \fB10\fR / \fB3\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-no-audit-log
disable the client's audit trail.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-fake-ctl set pv 2500
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-fake-ctl show settings
.IP \(bu 2
.B printf 'set pv 2500\\nset soc 30\\nshow status\\n' | modbus-fake-ctl
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every command answered \fBok\fR.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1),
.BR modbus-fake-cli (1)
